Spoiler warning:

The assumption is that you'v been "polypiling".  When a pile of objects is
zapped with a wand of polymorph, each object will (likely) change to another
object of similar type (weapons beget weapons, scrolls beget scrolls, etc.).

Make sure to throw all of the useless keys, extra pickaxes from murdered
dwarves, mirrors from nymphs, whistles, and whatever on the pile.  Each
tool has a chance at being polymorphed into a magic marker.

Serious polypilers have been known to pile hundreds of items on a pile, and
spend a long time at the whole thing.  Its fun (once or twice), but the
game is too easy once you're running around with all the goodies.

Some time ago I posted the results of a polypiling session that I did just
to prove how unbalanced the game becomes.  I had virtually every named
weapon (did need an altar), speed boots, all my attributes were maxed out,
I had all necessary intrinisics, etc., etc. all without going below level 10.
Ridiculous.  Needless to say, the rest of the game was too easy and boring.



